notes.content:
Storybook Setup — Technical Notes

Version: Storybook 8 (latest)
Framework: @storybook/nextjs (official integration)

Configuration Highlights:
- Auto-generates docs from TypeScript props
- Accessibility addon enabled (axe checks on every story)
- Dark mode toggle (tests both themes)
- Viewport presets (mobile, tablet, desktop)
- Interaction testing (play functions for complex states)

Story Format:
```typescript
import type { Meta, StoryObj } from '@storybook/react';
import { Button } from './Button';

const meta: Meta<typeof Button> = {
  component: Button,
  tags: ['autodocs'],
  argTypes: {
    variant: { control: 'select', options: ['primary', 'secondary', 'ghost'] },
  },
};

export default meta;
type Story = StoryObj<typeof Button>;

export const Primary: Story = {
  args: { children: 'Click me', variant: 'primary' },
};
```

Deployment:
- Storybook deploys to storybook.techflow.dev on every merge to main
- Chromatic for visual regression testing (screenshot comparison)
- Design team (Derek) uses Storybook as source of truth for implemented components

Maintenance:
- Lisa owns Storybook configuration
- Every new component MUST have at least: Default, All Variants, Accessibility story
- Review Storybook in each design sync with Derek
